# Release Notes: v1.1.0

**Release Date:** March 2026

## Overview

SonoPlay v1.1.0 is the first official release under the SonoPlay name. It covers everything built since the original plexdlnaplayer fork: virtual device groups for multi-room audio, a modern web UI, broad DLNA device compatibility, security hardening, accessibility, and stability improvements.

---

## What's New

### Virtual Device Groups
- Combine multiple DLNA speakers into synchronized multi-room groups
- Capability-based member validation ensures only compatible devices can be grouped
- Persistent storage maintains groups across restarts
- Dedicated web UI page and RESTful API for group management

### Modern Web UI
- Complete redesign from basic HTML table to responsive dual-page application
- Real-time device status, playback info, and statistics
- Mobile-friendly layouts with touch controls
- Search and filter across all device views

### DLNA Device Compatibility

#### Device Quirks System
- Per-device workaround registry with case-insensitive regex matching
- Built-in quirks for Sony, Denon/HEOS, Marantz, and Bose SoundTouch
- User overrides via `device_quirks` in data.json
- Sony-specific fixes: premature STOPPED filtering, wait-for-can-play polling

#### HTTP 5xx Retry Logic
- Oppo and similar devices that return HTTP 500 during normal operation now retry up to 3 times instead of failing immediately

#### XML Response Sanitization
- Pre-processes all XML responses to handle malformed output from various manufacturers

| Fix | Affected Devices |
|-----|------------------|
| Malformed namespace prefix (`<&` → `<s:`) | Oppo |
| Illegal XML control characters | Sonos |
| Missing `xmlns:dlna` declaration | Various |
| Non-standard namespace | Belkin WeMo |
| Trailing garbage after envelope | Various |
| Leading HTTP headers before XML | Windows UPnP |

### Security
- 14 CVEs resolved by bumping aiohttp, starlette, jinja2, brotli, and python-multipart
- XSS prevention — server-returned values in notification dialogs are properly escaped
- XML injection protection — device names escaped in generated XML; UUID inputs validated
- Dependency versions pinned for reproducible builds

### Accessibility
- Keyboard focus indicators (`focus-visible`)
- Reduced-motion support (`prefers-reduced-motion`)
- ARIA attributes on all interactive elements
- Semantic buttons and form labels throughout the UI

### Stability
- Proper shutdown cleanup — all background tasks (Plex TV, GDM discovery) cancelled on exit
- Thread-safe data access with locking on settings read/write
- Async-safe adapter and device removal
- Cross-thread `no_notice` race condition resolved
- Graceful device disconnect handling (503 status for unreachable devices)
- Subscriber eviction after 3 consecutive errors instead of 1

### Infrastructure
- Multi-stage Dockerfile with non-root container user
- Container healthcheck endpoint
- Deny-by-default `.dockerignore`
- GitHub Actions CI/CD — automatic image build and push to ghcr.io on tag
- Docker Compose support with named volumes

---

## Under the Hood

- Rebrand from SonoPlex → SonoPlay across all files
- Removed 2,300+ lines of dead frontend code (legacy theme system)
- Extracted shared JavaScript utilities into a single reusable module
- Deduplicated Plex HTTP header construction (3 copies → 1 shared builder)
- Subscription expiry tracking with proactive renewal
- Device statistics tracking (play count, total duration, session duration)

